At this point, we are ready to enroll other secrets into our LUKS device(s).
Hardware tokens generally provide stronger security than a plain passphrase
especially when they require additional unlocking with their own passphrase. As
part of this step, you will be able to unroll the following secrets:
    - a TPM2 device
    - a FIDO2 hardware token
    - a PKCS#11 hardware token
    - a random keyfile on a flash drive

After we have finalized our LUKS setup, we will create a backup of the LUKS
header, so you will be able to restore your data in case the header gets
corrupted.
